<!doctype html><html><head><title>Zero Web</title><style>body { background-color: #edf2f7; padding: 16px; } h1 { color: #0f766e; font-size: 32px; margin: 12px; } .card { background-color: #ffffff; padding: 16px; margin: 12px; } p { font-size: 16px; color: #243047; margin: 8px; } #result { color: #0f766e; } .hidden { display: none; }</style></head><body><h1>Zero Web</h1><div class=card><p>An original browser engine written in Zero.</p><p>HTML tree + CSS styles + bounded JavaScript.</p><p id=result>Waiting for the page script.</p><p class=hidden>This text must remain hidden.</p></div><div class=card><p>The engine draws every pixel using its own bitmap font.</p><p>Server-side Python, PHP or Ruby does not require a matching browser interpreter.</p></div><div class=card><p>Experimental preview: local documents, a limited web profile.</p><p>Not yet full HTML5, ECMAScript, HTTPS or Chromium compatibility.</p></div><script>const engine = 'Zero'; let features = 3; document.getElementById('result').textContent = engine + ': ' + features + ' engines ran successfully.';</script></body></html>